  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "Last summer \\(30\\%\\) of the birds living on Town Lake were geese, \\(25\\%\\) were swans, \\(10\\%\\) were herons, and \\(35\\%\\) were ducks. What percent of the birds that were not swans were geese?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(20\\)",
    "B": "\\(30\\)",
    "C": "\\(40\\)",
    "D": "\\(50\\)",
    "E": "\\(60\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The requested percentage uses the non-swans as its whole. Since \\(25\\%\\) of all birds were swans, \\(100\\%-25\\%=75\\%\\) were non-swans.\n\nAll geese belong to this group. Comparing their \\(30\\%\\) share of all birds with the \\(75\\%\\) non-swan share gives\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{75}=\\frac25=0.4=40\\%.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\boxed{40\\%}\\) of the non-swans were geese, choice C.",
